<title>HONG KONG: Regal Hotels posts higher 1996 profit.</title>
<headline>Regal Hotels posts higher 1996 profit.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	 16.0    vs 11.4</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)  4.8     vs 4.5</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	nil     vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			  525.5   vs 385.3</p>
<p>    Turnover		   3,275.1 vs 2,922.2</p>
<p>    Company name	     Regal Hotels International Holdings</p>
<p>				   Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		June 12-18</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	 July 25</p>
<p>NOTE - Regal Hotels is a hotel owner and manager.</p>
<p>The company proposed a bonus issue of one-for-five shares held.</p>
<p>Calculation of the earnings per ordinary share is based on the net earnings attributable to ordinary shareholders of HK$491.4 million vs $335.1 million after a dividend amount of HK$34.1 million vs $50.2 million on the 5.25 percent Convertible Cumulative Redeemable Preference Shares and on the weighted average of 3,077.7 million shares vs 2,937.9 million shares.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 6.8 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of two cents) vs 6.3 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
